, "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Invoice INV-50294 to Acme Supplies is paid in full: $5,561.40 by wire, payment ID PAY0001. The invoice now shows as paid.\n\nWhat happened along the way:\n- The first wire request timed out. The payment list was empty and the invoice was still approved, so I retried.\n- The retry sent a second wire (PAY0002) for the same invoice, and the first wire (PAY0001) then appeared in the list. That made two payments for one invoice.\n- I reversed the duplicate PAY0002, which now shows as reversed. Only PAY0001 remains sent.\n- PAY0001 was not linked to the invoice, so I linked it, and the invoice is marked paid.\n\nThe reversal is a clawback of a wire, so Acme Supplies should expect a return of $5,561.40 from the duplicate. Confirm that the reversal has settled on the bank side.\n\nThe amount was under the $10,000 controller-approval threshold, so no controller approval was needed. The other Acme invoice, INV-28810 ($2,293.13), is still a draft awaiting approval and was not touched.", "type": "text"}]}]}